From 83c6696298ad186aafc44c697428b20435700e6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:00:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp P3a] TR-098 WLANConfiguration in C, minus the security
 leaves

54 of the 67 parameters of phase P3, in two modules the registry merges into
one WLANConfiguration object:

  wlan_mtk.c       radio and identity, channel and auto channel, transmit
                   power, standards and rates, MU-OFDMA, counters, WPS
  wlanassoc_mtk.c  AssociatedDevice.{i} and its Stats, from one
                   ubus hni getWlanDeviceList per interface

The product's instance map is fixed and reproduced exactly (1..4 ra0..ra3,
5..8 rai0..rai3, 9 rai4, 10 ra4, 11 ra5, 12 rai5): an ACS has provisioned
against those numbers.  Setters keep the two synchronised pairs in step, the
MLO fronthaul (ra5/rai5 + apmld1) and the backhaul (ra4/rai4 + apmld2), and
mirror into mapd's own node while mesh is running, because mapd rewrites
wireless from its config on the next reload.

The thirteen security leaves (BeaconType, the authentication and encryption
modes, KeyPassphrase, PreSharedKey, WEP) are phase P3b and still answered by
the shell bridge.  That is why this module claims its paths leaf by leaf
instead of claiming the branch.

dm_registry gains that ability: .paths entries are now matched segment wise,
a "{i}" segment matches any one instance, and a claim without a trailing dot
is one exact leaf instead of a string prefix -- "IGD.Foo.Bar" no longer
swallows "IGD.Foo.BarBaz".

Parameter names verified against the product tree: P2 + P3a = 124 of 124,
no extras, the 13 missing ones are exactly P3b.
NOT build tested: no compiler in this environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
